# NestedText v3 — xhtml1-strict driver head (measured lines 1-60/966)
# Source: cc-resources/.dtd-file-examples/xhtml/dtd/xhtml1-strict.dtd

identity:
    public: -//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Strict//EN
    system: http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-strict.dtd
    namespace: http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml
    note: same as HTML4 Strict modulo XML-vs-SGML differences

entity-imports:
    - HTMLlat1: xhtml-lat1.ent (PUBLIC -//W3C//ENTITIES Latin 1 for XHTML//EN), invoked immediately via %HTMLlat1;
    - HTMLsymbol: xhtml-symbol.ent, invoked via %HTMLsymbol;
    - HTMLspecial: xhtml-special.ent
    pattern: declare-external-parameter-entity then invoke on next line — the include idiom behind svg .mod loading and our per-folder .nt includes

imported-names:
    - ContentType: CDATA (RFC2045 media type)
    - ContentTypes: CDATA (comma-separated list)
    - Charset: CDATA (RFC2045 encoding)
    - Charsets: CDATA (space-separated list)
    - LanguageCode: NMTOKEN (RFC3066)
    - Character: CDATA (single character per XML 2.2)

assimilation-note:
    > Typed-name pattern (ContentType vs ContentTypes, Charset vs Charsets) = precedent for Depth.dtd vs Type.dtd split: scalar vs list, each with its RFC-like authority note.
    > Strict vs transitional vs frameset diff still queued; .ent sample still queued.
